.TH BLK_MONITOR 1 "2026-05-21" "blk_monitor 1.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
blk_monitor \- monitor block device I/O activity and sync when idle
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B blk_monitor
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I /dev/sdX
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B blk_monitor
reads I/O counters from
.I /sys/block/<dev>/stat
at a configurable interval, tracks how long the device has been idle, and
runs
.BR sync (2)
once the idle duration is reached. It is a low-overhead, single-binary
replacement for shell loops that watch USB or external drives before unmount.

If a partition path is given
.RB ( /dev/sdb1 ", " /dev/nvme0n1p2 )
the parent block device is resolved automatically, since
.I /sys/block
only exposes whole-device stats.

.B blk_monitor
has no external dependencies beyond libc and works on any Linux kernel
2.6.26 or newer.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-interval " " \fISEC\fR
Poll interval in seconds. Range: 1\(en60. Default: 2.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-idle\-time " " \fISEC\fR
Required consecutive idle time in seconds before declaring the device safe.
Range: 5\(en3600. Default: 10.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-sync
Call
.BR sync (2)
before exiting (default).
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-no\-sync
Skip
.BR sync (2)
on exit. Useful for monitor-only mode or unprivileged runs.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress the live UI; only the final status line is printed.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print one line per poll instead of the in-place progress bar.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Emit one JSON object per poll on stdout, plus a terminal
.RI { \(dqevent\(dq:\(dqidle\(dq,... }
line when the idle threshold is reached. stdout is line-buffered, so
consumers (e.g.
.BR jq (1) )
see each record immediately.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI colors. Colors are also disabled automatically when stdout
is not a terminal or when the
.B NO_COLOR
environment variable is set.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Device became idle for the required duration (and was synced if
.B -s
was enabled).
.TP
.B 1
Error: invalid arguments, device not found / not a block device, read or
write failure.
.TP
.B 2
Interrupted by
.B SIGINT
or
.B SIGTERM
before the idle threshold was reached.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set (to any value), ANSI colors are disabled, as if
.B -C
were passed. See
.UR https://no\-color.org
.UE .

.SH EXAMPLES
Monitor a USB drive with default timings:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
sudo blk_monitor /dev/sdb
.fi
.RE
.PP
Quick mode \(en check every second, declare safe after 5\ s idle:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
sudo blk_monitor -i 1 -t 5 /dev/sdb
.fi
.RE
.PP
Pass a partition; the parent device is resolved automatically:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
sudo blk_monitor /dev/nvme0n1p2
.fi
.RE
.PP
Stream JSON to
.BR jq (1)
in real time:
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
sudo blk_monitor -j --no-sync -i 1 -t 5 /dev/sdb | jq -c .
.fi
.RE

.SH FILES
.TP
.I /sys/block/<dev>/stat
The kernel's per-device I/O counters. The 11-field format introduced in
Linux 2.6.26 is required.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sync (2),
.BR sync (8),
.BR umount (8),
.BR udisks (8),
.BR losetup (8)

